{
  "$comment": [
    "The ledger of what the catalogue model of ADR-0225 retires, read by scripts/lint-retired-model.mjs (lint:retired, docs/tech/gates.md § The retired model).",
    "An entry names what goes, by `names` (each matched as a whole identifier) and, where a name alone cannot say it, by `pattern` (a JavaScript regular expression, tested line by line).",
    "`floor: true` marks an entry whose name is shared with something the model keeps, so its count is a floor; before a slice flips it to retired, its pattern finds every use it retires.",
    "`state` is `retired` once the slice that retires it has merged: from then on any mention outside `allow` fails the gate. A `pending` entry is the slice's debt, printed as a count and never failed.",
    "A slice flips its entries to `retired` in the pull request that retires them. `allow` holds the deliberate mentions, each with its reason; one that matches no line fails the gate."
  ],
